  "query_preview": "..\n(Monday night through next Saturday)\nIssued at 1014 PM CDT Sat Aug 1 2026\n\nA generally uneventful pattern will continue for much of next week. \nThe aforementioned high pressure very slowly shifts to the west, \nand the general forecast should remain essentially unchanged from\nday-to-day. Highs will be slightly cooler than last week, however\nstill may reach near 105 off the Caprock. Storm chances cannot \ncompletely be ruled out but look to be minimal/isolated, although \nmay slightly increase towards the end of the week as the ridge \ntracks farther west bringing potential convective development with\nembedded shortwaves on its eastern periphery.",
